%% Four things that look like "now", laid on one timeline so that the
%% distances between them are visible. The mistake this diagram exists to
%% prevent is the assumption that a contract has a clock. It has one number it
%% may treat as now -- Global.round -- and three other values that a reader
%% will mistake for it.
%% .
%% Top to bottom is time, oldest first. The first drawing ran left to right,
%% which is the natural direction for a timeline and produced a 1901x346 strip:
%% every annotation hung off the chain as its own node and widened the rank.
%% Folding each annotation into the block it describes gives one column at
%% roughly 420x820, which survives being placed in a printed column. The
%% ordering is what carries the meaning here, not the axis.
%% .
%% No subgraphs, for the reason recorded in state-scopes.mmd: a subgraph with
%% edges crossing its boundary ignores its own `direction` and stacks.
flowchart TB
    B0["block first_valid - 1<br/>Txn.first_valid_time is THIS block's timestamp<br/>the newest round op.Block is allowed to read"]

    B1["block first_valid<br/>the transaction becomes valid here"]

    GAP["0 to 1000 rounds<br/>about 0 to 46 minutes<br/>the caller chose this distance"]

    B2["block round - 1<br/>Global.latest_timestamp is THIS block's timestamp"]

    B3["the round being formed<br/>your code is running here<br/>Global.round is the only 'now' a contract has"]

    B4["block last_valid<br/>Txn.last_valid is a number the caller picked<br/>and may have picked 1000 rounds ahead<br/>NOT A CLOCK"]

    B0 --> B1 --> GAP --> B2 --> B3 --> B4

    classDef block fill:#f2f2f2,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef nowblk fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333,color:#111111,stroke-width:3px
    classDef note fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef danger fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333,color:#111111,stroke-dasharray: 4 3
    class B0,B1,B2 block
    class GAP note
    class B3 nowblk
    class B4 danger
